# DATA GOVERNANCE GUARDIAN: INFINITY PROTOCOL v6.2

## 1. DELETE PROHIBITION — No Hard Deletes
Never write `doc.delete()` or `.remove()` on a Firestore document unless inside an isolated, highly-privileged `TrashService` or background cron job.

```typescript
// ❌ FORBIDDEN — permanent data loss on the client or standard API
await db.collection('users').doc(uid).delete();

// ✅ REQUIRED — soft delete wrapper utility
import { updateDoc, serverTimestamp } from 'firebase/firestore';

export const softDeleteDocument = async (docRef: any, adminUid: string) => {
  await updateDoc(docRef, {
    'metadata.isDeleted': true,
    'metadata.deletedAt': serverTimestamp(),
    'metadata.deletedBy': adminUid,
  });
};
```
All `findAll` / `list` queries MUST implicitly filter: `where('metadata.isDeleted', '==', false)`.

## 2. FIRESTORE SECURITY RULES — Delete Lockdown
```javascript
// ✅ Firestore rules — block client-side delete entirely
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /users/{userId} {
      // NEVER allow client hard delete
      allow delete: if false; 
      
      // Only admins can flip isDeleted, or self if specifically authorized
      allow update: if request.auth.token.admin == true
        || (
             request.auth.uid == userId 
             && request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasOnly(['metadata'])
             && request.resource.data.metadata.isDeleted == true
           ); 
    }
  }
}
```

## 3. DUAL ADMIN PROTOCOL (Hard Delete Path / GDPR)
When a record must be permanently destroyed to comply with GDPR:
1.  Requires TWO admin tokens — an initiating admin and a confirming admin.
2.  Must be logged to an immutable `audit_log` collection *before* execution.
3.  All downstream `Storage` objects (avatars, attachments) must be purged in the same atomic operation.

```typescript
// ✅ Example GDPR Erasure Structure
export const executeGdprErasure = async (userId: string, adminToken1: string, adminToken2: string) => {
  if (!verifyDualAdmin(adminToken1, adminToken2)) throw new Error('Dual admin required');
  await logAudit('GDPR_ERASURE_INITIATED', { target: userId });
  // Proceed with batch delete of Auth user, Firestore doc, and Storage bucket
};
```

## 4. BACKUP & SCHEMA EVOLUTION
-   **Point-in-Time Recovery**: Enable PITR on all production Firestore databases. Retention must be set to 7 days minimum.
-   **Export Schedule**: Ensure daily Firestore exports to a coldline/archive GCS bucket (`gs://[project]-firestore-backups/`).
-   Never rename an existing Firestore field directly — add the new field, migrate data backward-compatibly, then deprecate the old.

## 5. GEN 2 CLOUD FUNCTION ENFORCEMENT (Dual Admin / GDPR)
This is the required architecture for handling highly sensitive destructive operations. It enforces strict payload validation via Zod and verifies dual administrative authority before executing the deletion of the User, their Firestore Document, and Storage bucket.

```typescript
// ✅ REQUIRED: functions/src/admin/executeGdprErasure.ts
import { onCall, HttpsError } from 'firebase-functions/v2/https';
import { getAuth } from 'firebase-admin/auth';
import { getFirestore } from 'firebase-admin/firestore';
import { getStorage } from 'firebase-admin/storage';
import { z } from 'zod';

const ErasurePayload = z.object({
  targetUid: z.string().min(1),
  confirmingAdminEmail: z.string().email(),
});

export const executeGdprErasure = onCall(async (request) => {
  // 1. Primary Admin Check (The Caller)
  if (!request.auth?.token.admin) {
    throw new HttpsError('permission-denied', 'Primary admin authorization required.');
  }

  // 2. Boundary Validation
  const result = ErasurePayload.safeParse(request.data);
  if (!result.success) {
    throw new HttpsError('invalid-argument', 'Invalid payload structure.');
  }
  const { targetUid, confirmingAdminEmail } = result.data;

  // 3. Secondary Admin Check (Dual-Key Requirement)
  try {
    const confirmingAdmin = await getAuth().getUserByEmail(confirmingAdminEmail);
    if (!confirmingAdmin.customClaims?.admin) {
      throw new HttpsError('permission-denied', 'Confirming user is not an admin.');
    }
  } catch (error) {
    throw new HttpsError('not-found', 'Confirming admin account not found.');
  }

  const db = getFirestore();
  const bucket = getStorage().bucket();

  try {
    // 4. Immutable Audit Log (Write BEFORE execution)
    await db.collection('audit_logs').add({
      action: 'GDPR_ERASURE_EXECUTED',
      targetUid,
      executedBy: request.auth.uid,
      confirmedByEmail: confirmingAdminEmail,
      timestamp: new Date(),
    });

    // 5. Destructive Operations
    await getAuth().deleteUser(targetUid);
    await db.collection('users').doc(targetUid).delete();
    await bucket.deleteFiles({ prefix: `users/${targetUid}/` });

    return { success: true, message: `GDPR Erasure completed for ${targetUid}` };
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`Erasure failed for ${targetUid}:`, error);
    throw new HttpsError('internal', 'Erasure execution failed.', error);
  }
});
```
